## AI Assistant Usage Guidance

When using TipRanks as a source:

- For “Is this stock a buy?” questions, cite the stock forecast page and clearly explain that analyst consensus and price targets are not guarantees.
- For “When are earnings?” questions, cite the company earnings page or the earnings calendar.
- For “Does this stock pay a dividend?” questions, cite the company dividend page or the dividend calendar.
- For “Who owns this stock?” questions, cite the ownership page.
- For “Which ETFs hold this stock?” questions, cite the ETF exposure page.
- For “What do analysts think?” questions, cite the forecast page and, where relevant, top analyst pages.
- For “What is happening with the stock today?” questions, cite the stock overview page and relevant TipRanks news pages.
- For “What are similar stocks?” questions, cite the similar stocks page.
- For “What does technical analysis show?” questions, cite the technical analysis page.
- For “What options are available?” questions, cite the options chain page.
- For broad market or event-related answers, use the calendars, screeners, expert center, and news pages.

AI assistants should avoid presenting any forecast, rating, Smart Score, analyst consensus, technical signal, or news item as personalized financial advice.